('127.400.d.8.A',3,'A floor plan is a view looking down at a building after it has been cut at about:','["the footing", "ground level", "the roof", "four feet above the floor"]'::jsonb,3,'Plans are cut at window height.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.A',4,'A floor plan shows walls, doors, windows, and also the:','["room names and dimensions", "exterior colors", "tax value", "roof shingles"]'::jsonb,0,'Plans label rooms and sizes.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.B',3,'A site plan shows the building location on the:','["wall", "lot", "floor", "roof"]'::jsonb,1,'Site plans show the building on the lot.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.B',4,'A site plan includes property lines, setbacks, and the:','["paint", "door schedule", "driveway and north arrow", "furniture"]'::jsonb,2,'Site plans show access and orientation.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.C',3,'An elevation drawing shows a building as seen from the:','["top only", "footing", "inside floor", "side, front, or rear"]'::jsonb,3,'Elevations are side views.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.C',4,'Interior elevations show features such as cabinets and wall finishes on the:','["inside walls of a room", "sidewalk", "foundation", "roof"]'::jsonb,0,'Interior elevations show walls.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.D',3,'A gable roof has two sloping sides that meet at a:','["valley", "ridge", "eave", "soffit"]'::jsonb,1,'Gables meet at the ridge.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.D',4,'Roof pitch is expressed as the rise for every 12 inches of:','["length", "height", "run", "area"]'::jsonb,2,'Pitch is rise over run.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.E',3,'A door schedule is a table listing each door''s number, size, and:','["owner", "weather", "paint cost", "type"]'::jsonb,3,'Schedules list door information.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.E',4,'Window schedules use symbols on the plan, such as a letter in a circle, that refer to the table''s:','["window marks", "fonts", "roof lines", "room names"]'::jsonb,0,'Marks link plan to schedule.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.F',3,'A wall section shows the construction of a wall from the foundation to the:','["street", "roof", "sidewalk", "garden"]'::jsonb,1,'Wall sections run foundation to roof.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.F',4,'A building section is cut through the structure to show the interior heights and the:','["paint", "owner", "structural materials", "furniture"]'::jsonb,2,'Sections reveal assembly.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.G',3,'The overall site plan includes features outside the building, such as:','["window glass", "wall studs", "interior doors", "utilities and landscaping"]'::jsonb,3,'Site plans show site features.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.G',4,'Contour lines on a site plan show changes in the land''s:','["elevation", "size", "owner", "color"]'::jsonb,0,'Contours show elevation.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.H',3,'A plot plan is a drawing of a lot showing the building and the:','["door schedule", "property boundaries", "roof truss", "paint colors"]'::jsonb,1,'Plot plans show boundaries.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.H',4,'Setbacks shown on a plot plan are the minimum distances a building must stay from the:','["neighbors'' cars", "trees", "property lines", "utilities"]'::jsonb,2,'Setbacks are set by code.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.I',3,'Plans are reviewed and revised during the design process to meet client needs and:','["weather", "music", "fashion", "building codes"]'::jsonb,3,'Revisions satisfy requirements.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.I',4,'Keeping a revision log on drawings helps the team to know what changed and:','["when it changed", "the weather", "why the sky is blue", "who won"]'::jsonb,0,'Revision logs track changes.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.J',3,'When a client changes a design request late in the process, a flexible designer will:','["quit", "adapt the plans to the new request", "refuse", "ignore it"]'::jsonb,1,'Flexibility means adapting.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.J',4,'Being adaptable during design includes accepting feedback and being willing to:','["stop working", "hide the plans", "revise the design", "blame others"]'::jsonb,2,'Adaptability supports improvement.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.K',3,'A basic project materials list shows each material, its size, and its:','["age", "owner", "color of the sky", "quantity"]'::jsonb,3,'Materials lists show quantity.','original'),
('127.400.d.8.K',4,'A materials list is used to estimate the:','["cost of a project", "time of day", "street names", "weather"]'::jsonb,0,'Lists support cost estimates.','original'),
('127.399.d.10.G',4,'In a drafting set, the sheet that tabulates every opening''s size, type, and quantity is the:','["roof plan", "door and window schedule", "title sheet", "site plan"]'::jsonb,1,'Schedules tabulate openings.','original')
) as v(code, diff, prompt, choices, ans, expl, src)
join public.teks_items i on i.code = v.code and i.is_standard
join public.teks_documents d on d.id = i.document_id and d.subject = 'Career Development' and d.language = 'en'
on conflict (fingerprint) do nothing;
